---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Convocados"
  description="What Convocados collects, why, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to export or delete it."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      Convocados is a game-organising app run by José Cabeda ("we", "us"). This page
      covers the website, the Android apps and the MCP server at
      <code>https://convocados.cabeda.dev/api/mcp</code>. It explains what we collect,
      why, who processes it, how long we keep it, and how to get it back or delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account:</strong> your name, email address, a password hash if you sign in
        with email, or your Google account identifier if you sign in with Google, plus a
        profile image when your provider supplies one.</li>
      <li><strong>Games and play:</strong> the games you create or join, rosters, RSVPs,
        teams, scores, Elo ratings, and the costs and payment records you or an organiser
        enter. Some of this is about other people — an organiser adds players by name.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> push subscription details when you enable push,
        your notification preferences, and the email address we send reminders to.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical:</strong> a session cookie that keeps you signed in, your IP
        address used in memory for rate limiting, and any API keys or calendar feed tokens
        you create.</li>
      <li><strong>Assistant access:</strong> if you connect an AI assistant over MCP, an
        OAuth token scoped to the permissions you approve, and a record of that approval.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not run third-party analytics or advertising trackers, and we do not sell
      personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To run the app: sign you in, show your games, keep rosters, scores and ratings
        correct, and send the notifications you asked for.</li>
      <li>To keep it safe and working: rate limiting, abuse prevention, and a log of
        changes to games so a mistake can be traced.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who processes it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fly.io</strong> — hosting and the disk the database lives on.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare R2</strong> — encrypted database backups.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email: sign-in links, invites, reminders.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> — sign-in, only if you choose it.</li>
      <li><strong>Browser push services and Firebase Cloud Messaging</strong> — push
        notifications, only if you enable them.</li>
      <li><strong>Playtomic</strong> — court availability, only when you use Court Finder.</li>
      <li><strong>The assistant you connect</strong> (for example Anthropic's Claude) —
        receives the result of each tool it calls, under that provider's own terms.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each of these processes data on our behalf, except Google and the assistant
      provider, which you also have your own agreement with.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Your account and the games attached to it are kept while your account exists. Backups
      roll over on a short cycle after a deletion. Rate-limit counters are discarded within
      minutes.
    </p>

    <h2>Exporting and deleting</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Export:</strong> <code>GET /api/me/export</code> returns a JSON copy of
        your account and the games you take part in.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete:</strong> in the app, Profile → Delete account, or
        <code>DELETE /api/me/account</code>. This removes your user record, sign-in
        accounts, sessions, API keys and calendar tokens, and detaches your player entries
        and ratings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      What stays: games, rosters, scores and ratings belong to the group you played with, so
      deleting your account does not erase the other players' history. Your entries are
      detached from your account, but the player name your group knows you by remains in
      that history. Games you owned are kept, without an owner, so the group can still play
      them.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      One first-party session cookie keeps you signed in. There are no advertising or
      cross-site tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Convocados is not intended for anyone under 16.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When this policy changes we update this page and the date at the top. Material changes
      are announced in the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or a request about your data: <a href="mailto:cabeda@proton.me">cabeda@proton.me</a>.
      See also <a href="/docs/mcp">the MCP server documentation</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

